{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And all that walks on its paws.</b> At the outset the ruling is one, and likewise [regarding] 'one who carries their carcass.' This verse confirms my interpretation of the phrase 'and by these you shall become impure,' for there it is written 'and all who carry from their carcass,' and both are in one pericope." "The sense of <b>they are impure to you</b> is to include all Israel, men and women and children, under one ruling for them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:35.581635898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}